{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-326294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5{c}_{1}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2\\cdot 1+{c}_{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89ff37eb35ec8c1ba12426d1ac9dd8c7ed420a07f95af35c6e904141d57a9a35"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326294" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $-2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-7{c}_{2}=-7\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89ff37eb35ec8c1ba12426d1ac9dd8c7ed420a07f95af35c6e904141d57a9a35"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326002" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5{c}_{2}=10\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2\\cdot 2=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3e6f71ba99792efe1d70ef7"} {"question" "q-326295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89ff37eb35ec8c1ba12426d1ac9dd8c7ed420a07f95af35c6e904141d57a9a35"} {"question" "q-326295" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067494/state.json" "file_sha256" "83532cd8775da02f680d928be9e2f1005c5182bcc3